# A NAK refuses the whole batch, so its caps are asked for again one at a
# time and only the one the server really lacks is lost.
= caps away-notify bogus-cap multi-prefix
> CAP LS 302
> NICK textual
> USER textual 0 * Textual
< :ergo.test CAP * LS :away-notify bogus-cap multi-prefix
> CAP REQ :away-notify bogus-cap multi-prefix
< :ergo.test CAP * NAK :away-notify bogus-cap multi-prefix
> CAP REQ away-notify
> CAP REQ bogus-cap
> CAP REQ multi-prefix
< :ergo.test CAP * ACK away-notify
< :ergo.test CAP * NAK bogus-cap
< :ergo.test CAP * ACK multi-prefix
> CAP END
< :ergo.test 001 textual :Welcome
? registered textual
